/* 段落记忆 · 词层 5 · 子块 b：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(5,{"sub":"b","par":{"fury":{"tw":[["furious",4],["rage",0],["wrath",3],["anger",2],["shock",6],["infuriate",4],["frenzy",0],["mania",2],["outrage",6],["craze",0]],"en":"A craze for the new buns swept our street this month, and every morning a long queue formed before the shop opened. On Tuesday the last tray sold out while I was still third in line, and a man behind me was furious. His rage was out of all proportion: he shouted at the girl at the counter until the whole queue stood in shock. Such anger over bread seemed comic, but his wrath did not stop, and his shouting began to infuriate even the patient regulars. For a minute the shop became a frenzy of raised voices, and an old woman said his outrage was mania over nothing. Then the oven timer rang, a fresh tray came out, and the fury died as quickly as it had risen. He bought six buns, apologized twice, and everyone laughed.","zh":"这个月我们街上刮起了一阵新出炉面包的风潮，每天早上店门还没开就排起了长队。周二最后一盘卖完时，我才排第三，身后一个男子火冒三丈。他的怒气大得离谱：冲着柜台的女孩嚷，整条队都惊呆了。为几个面包生这么大气看着有点好笑，可他的火气停不下来，连耐心的老主顾都被他惹恼了。有那么一分钟，店里乱成一片吼声的狂潮，一位老太太说他这通发火简直没来由地疯了。然后烤箱计时器响了，新的一盘端出来，那股狂怒来得快去得也快。他买了六个面包，道了两回歉，大家都笑了。"},"intrude":{"tw":[["intrusion",4],["nose",0],["bother",3],["enter",2],["encroach",6],["intrusive",4],["poke",0],["search",2],["impinge",6],["pry",0]],"en":"When my sister moved her desk into my room, her habits began to intrude on every quiet hour I had. She would enter without knocking, poke her nose into my drawers in search of her lost pens, and pry into every message that lit up my screen. At first I said nothing, because a little intrusion is normal in a family. But her questions grew intrusive, and her boxes began to encroach on half of my desk. What bothered me most was the way her chores always landed at the same hour and impinged on my study time. So I asked her to bother me only after dinner, and to search for her pens in her own room. She agreed, and to my surprise she has kept her word.","zh":"姐姐把书桌搬进我房间以后，她的习惯开始闯进我每一个安静的钟点。她进门不敲门，翻我的抽屉找她弄丢的笔，还爱打探我屏幕上亮起的每条消息。起初我什么也没说，毕竟一家人有点小打扰很正常。可她的问题越来越让人不适，她的纸箱也渐渐占掉我半张桌子。最让我心烦的是她的家务活总挑同一个钟点来，正好压在我的学习时间上。于是我请她晚饭之后再来打扰我，笔也回她自己房间找。她答应了，而且出乎意料，她说到做到。"},"globe":{"tw":[["global",4],["ball",0],["pellet",3],["model",2],["press",6],["earth",0],["globule",3],["sphere",2],["watch",6],["world",0]],"en":"At the technology fair, one stand showed a smart globe that could display the weather of any place on earth. The screen was a perfect sphere, and a small ball inside floated like a silver pellet in a drop of water. A student pressed a button and the model turned slowly, showing storms moving across the world. Reporters from the local press watched, and so did a crowd of schoolchildren who had come with their teacher. The maker explained that the global data came from satellites every hour, so the image you see is almost live. One child asked why the floating globule never fell, and the answer made the whole stand laugh. It was the cleverest display of the day, and I stood there until the hall closed.","zh":"在科技展会上，有一个展台展示了一台智能地球仪，它能显示地球上任何地方的天气。屏幕是一个完美的球体，里面悬浮着一颗小球，像水滴里的一粒银色小珠。一个学生按下按钮，模型缓缓转动，展示着风暴在世界各地移动的过程。本地媒体的记者在一旁观看，跟着老师来的一群小学生也在看。制作者解释说，全球数据每小时都从卫星传回，所以你看到的画面几乎是实时的。有个小孩问那颗悬浮的小珠为什么永远不掉下来，答案让整个展台都笑了。这是当天最巧妙的展示，我一直站到展厅关门。"},"dominance":{"tw":[["dominant",4],["control",2],["command",3],["condition",2],["supremacy",6],["dominate",4],["dominion",3],["advantage",6]],"en":"In our book club one member had built such dominance that nobody else dared to disagree. He would take command of every meeting, interrupt the shy ones, and dominate even the smallest discussion about tea. His advantage was clear: he read faster and spoke with more confidence than the rest of us. Two friends complained, but only on the condition that their names were not mentioned. At last the group agreed on a simple rule about control of the floor: each speaker gets ten minutes, and the loudest voice has no supremacy anymore. He seemed surprised, then laughed and accepted his less dominant role with good grace. Since then the talk flows both ways, and even the quietest member has begun to hold her own small dominion over the second Thursday of the month.","zh":"在我们的读书会上，有位成员积攒起了十足的支配力，别人都不敢反驳。他每次聚会都要发号施令，打断腼腆的人，连关于茶的小话题也要由他主导。他的优势很明显：读得比大家快，说得也更有底气。两位朋友提过意见，但条件是不要说出他们的名字。最后大家定下一条关于发言权的简单规矩：每人十分钟，嗓门最大的人从此不再独占上风。他先是意外，随后笑着体面地接受了这个不那么强势的角色。从那以后，谈话能双向流动，连最安静的成员也开始在每月第二个周四的讨论里守住属于自己的一方天地。"},"divert":{"tw":[["diversion",4],["amuse",0],["route",3],["send",2],["deflect",6],["deviate",3],["detour",3],["entertain",2],["seize",6]],"en":"The main route to the shopping street was closed for repairs, so every bus had to divert through the old market lane. The detour added ten minutes, but it turned into an unexpected diversion: a street musician had gathered a crowd and would amuse the waiting passengers with an old song. While we were held there, a shop assistant came out to send flyers to anyone who would take one, and a juggler seized the chance to entertain us too. I had planned to buy only rice and tea, but I deviated from my list completely and came home with a hat, two candles, and a kite. My sister tried to deflect the blame onto the closed road, but honestly nobody in our house minded. Sometimes the long way round is the better route.","zh":"通往购物街的主路封闭整修，每班公交都只好改道穿过老市场小巷。绕路多花了十分钟，却成了一场意外的消遣：一位街头艺人聚起人群，用一首老歌逗笑等候的乘客。我们被困在那儿时，店员出来给愿意接的人发传单，一个玩杂耍的也抓住机会给我们表演。我本来只打算买米和茶，却完全偏离了购物单，回家时多了一顶帽子、两根蜡烛和一只风筝。姐姐想把责任推给封闭的路，可说实话，家里没人在意。有时候绕远路反而是更好的路线。"},"expel":{"tw":[["expulsion",4],["exhaust",0],["blow",3],["move",2],["release",0],["emit",3],["remove",2],["discharge",0]],"en":"On Sunday afternoon I settled down at my desk to rebuild my weekly plan and to expel every habit that was stealing my time. First came the expulsion of two pointless meetings; I asked if they could move into a shared email instead. My old laptop helped in its own way: its fan would exhaust hot air, emit a tired hum, and discharge its battery twice as fast as it should. I removed three apps that did nothing but send me alerts, and the machine finally went quiet. A cold wind began to blow outside, so I closed the window and released the rest of the evening to real work. Two hours later the new schedule was done, and it left whole mornings free. The relief was immediate; sometimes the best plan is simply a shorter one.","zh":"周日下午，我在书桌前坐定，重新规划一周安排，并把每个偷走我时间的坏习惯都清除出去。首先是把两个毫无意义的会议逐出日程——我提议它们改成共享邮件就行。我的旧笔记本也用自己的方式帮了忙：它的风扇排着热气，发出疲惫的嗡嗡声，电池掉电的速度快得不像话。我删掉了三个只会给我发提醒的应用，机器总算安静了。外面刮起了冷风，我关上窗，把晚上剩下的时间交还给真正的工作。两个小时后新计划表完成，整整齐齐空出了好几个上午。轻松感立竿见影；有时候最好的计划就是更短的计划。"},"hawk":{"tw":[["hawking",4],["pitch",0],["board",2],["dove",1],["helicopter",6],["peddle",0],["deal",2],["eagle",6],["vend",0]],"en":"On the second day of our coastal trip, we walked along the pier while passengers were boarding the little ferry. A souvenir seller was hawking her postcards near the railing, another man tried to peddle straw hats, and a third would vend cold drinks from a cart, each with the same cheerful pitch. Above the noise a hawk circled in slow rings, and far over the water someone thought they saw an eagle. A dove rested under the steps, oddly calm with all the sellers around. A sightseeing helicopter passed twice and drowned every call for a minute. We made a small deal for four cold juices at half price, then stood watching the birds and the sea until the light turned gold. The ferry blew its horn, and we still had not moved.","zh":"海岸之行的第二天，我们沿着码头散步，那时小渡船正在让乘客登船。栏杆边有个小贩在兜售明信片，另一个男人在推销草帽，还有一辆推车卖冷饮，每个人的吆喝都同样欢快。喧闹声之上，一只鹰慢悠悠地盘旋，海面远处有人说自己看见了雕。台阶下歇着一只鸽子，周围叫卖声不断，它却出奇地安稳。观光直升机飞过两趟，有那么一分钟压过了所有叫卖声。我们以半价讲下四杯冷饮的小买卖，然后站着看鸟看海，直到天色变金。渡船鸣了笛，我们却还没挪步。"},"dismay":{"tw":[["alarm",0],["shock",3],["fear",2],["anger",6],["depress",0],["chill",3],["despair",2],["disgust",6],["appal",0]],"en":"When the first frost came early, the gardeners looked at the black rows in dismay. The alarm had been sounded the night before, but few had time to cover anything. The shock of losing a season of work was plain on every face. Some felt anger at the forecast, others a quiet fear that slid into despair. The cold would chill the ground for weeks and depress even the strongest plants. One old woman said the sight filled her with disgust, though she came back the next morning to dig. Such a loss would appal anyone who had planted those seeds by hand. By noon the sun had melted the thin white layer, and the damage looked worse than before.","zh":"初霜来得早，种园子的人望着发黑的一畦畦菜，心里一片沮丧。前一晚已经有人示警，可几乎没人来得及盖上什么。一季的活计就这么没了，那种打击写在每个人脸上。有人怨预报不准，有人心里悄悄生出一层恐惧，慢慢变成绝望。寒气会把地冻上好几个星期，连最壮实的苗也压得抬不起头。一位老太太说这景象让她心里发腻，可第二天早上她还是回来翻土。这样的损失，凡是亲手播过那些种子的人都会觉得震惊。到中午太阳化掉了那层薄白，灾情看着比先前更糟。"},"dissent":{"tw":[["protest",0],["strike",3],["oppose",2],["assent",1],["stifle",6],["resist",0],["contradict",3],["outcry",6],["disagree",2]],"en":"At the factory meeting, one worker dared to voice dissent about the new shift plan. Her protest was calm, but it was enough to make the room quiet. The manager asked whether anyone would oppose the change, and a few hands went up. Others chose to assent, because they feared the loss of overtime. The union tried to stifle the discussion before it spread to the whole floor. Still, a small group would resist the plan and contradict the figures in the report. By evening there was an outcry in the local paper, and a strike was mentioned for the first time. Not everyone who disagreed wanted to walk out.","zh":"在厂里的会上，一个工人壮着胆子对新的倒班方案提了异议。她的反对很平静，却足以让整个屋子安静下来。经理问还有谁反对这项变动，有几只手举了起来。另一些人选择同意，因为他们怕丢了加班费。工会想在这场讨论传遍整个车间之前把它压下去。可还是有一小拨人坚持抵制这个方案，并逐条驳斥报告里的数字。到了傍晚，本地报纸上已经有人大声抗议，头一回有人提到罢工。并不是每个不同意的人都愿意撂下活儿走人。"},"expire":{"tw":[["die",0],["blow",3],["breathe",2],["postpone",6],["pass",0],["fall",3],["discontinue",2],["freeze",6],["choke",0]],"en":"My uncle's licence to sell fish at the market would expire at the end of March. He had asked the office to postpone the renewal, but no answer came. Without the paper he could not breathe easily, and every morning he would blow on his cold hands and wait. A rumour said the old rules would die with the new year and the whole row would fall. He watched two neighbouring stalls discontinue their trade and choke on their debts. The pipes in the yard would freeze at night, and he had to pass a bucket of hot water along the wall. On the last day he signed the form at the desk, and the worry seemed to pass.","zh":"我叔叔在市场卖鱼的执照三月底就到期。他请办事处把换证的事往后拖一拖，可一直没有回音。没有那张纸，他连气都喘不顺，每天早上只能往冻僵的手上哈气，然后等着。有传言说旧规矩过了年就作废，整排摊子都要垮。他眼看着隔壁两家收了摊，被债压得喘不上气。院子里的水管夜里会上冻，他只好提着一桶热水沿着墙根浇过去。最后一天他在柜台前签了表，那份愁才算过去了。"},"flutter":{"tw":[["bat",0],["stir",3],["beat",2],["frown",6],["flap",0],["storm",3],["wave",2],["clap",6],["fleet",0]],"en":"A grey moth was caught inside the barn, and its flutter against the lamp kept us awake. A bat came in through the open door and began to beat the air above our heads. Its wings were dusty and torn, and it had been in the barn for two days. Every flap of its wings would stir the dust and make the lamp sway. Outside, the storm pushed the tall grass into a slow wave across the field. Down at the harbour a fleet of small boats had come in long before. My aunt would frown at the noise and clap her hands to drive the bat out. In the morning the moth lay still on the sill, and the barn was quiet again.","zh":"一只灰蛾被困在谷仓里，扑着灯罩，弄得我们睡不着。一只蝙蝠从敞开的门飞进来，在我们头顶上拍打空气。它的翅膀又脏又破，看来在仓里待了两天。它每扇一下翅膀，就把灰尘搅起来，灯也跟着晃。外面风暴把高草推成一道缓慢的浪，从田里扫过去。港口那边，一小队船早就进港了。我姑妈听着这动静直皱眉，拍着手想把蝙蝠赶出去。天亮时蛾子静静躺在窗台上，谷仓又安静了。"},"foam":{"tw":[["sparkle",0],["head",3],["material",2],["plastic",6],["froth",0],["seethe",3],["bubble",2],["glue",6],["fizz",0]],"en":"In the shed by the harbour, my cousin would cut a sheet of foam to fit the seat of an old boat. The material was light, and a little plastic glue held it in place. He had ordered the sheet months ago, and it had come by truck from a town inland. Outside, the tide would seethe around the rocks and throw a white froth onto the steps. Small bubbles would rise and fizz along the water line, and the surface would sparkle in the morning light. He said the foam saved weight and kept the head of every wave off the deck. When the wind dropped, only a thin line of foam was left on the sand.","zh":"在港口边那间棚子里，我表哥会裁一块泡沫塑料，给一条旧船配座垫。这种材料很轻，一点塑料胶就能把它固定住。这块料是他几个月前订的，用卡车从内陆一个镇子运来。外面潮水在礁石间翻腾，把白色的沫子甩到台阶上。小气泡沿着水线往上冒、嘶嘶地破，水面在晨光里闪亮。他说泡沫既省重量，又能挡住浪头，不让水打到甲板上。风一停，沙滩上只剩薄薄一线泡沫。"},"foil":{"tw":[["cross",0],["ruin",3],["cover",2],["wrap",6],["frustrate",0],["slide",3],["picture",2],["pan",6],["spoil",0]],"en":"My mother would wrap the fish in foil with a little salt and lemon, then slide the pan into the oven. She said the silver sheet kept the flesh soft and stopped the skin from drying. Once a guest tried to spoil the meal by arriving late with a cold dish, but her calm manner was a foil to his temper. He wanted to cross her at every turn and frustrate her plans, yet she only smiled. A torn piece of foil could ruin the whole tray if it let the steam escape. She would cover the top with a second sheet and slide it back in. The picture on the old box showed a dish far grander than ours.","zh":"我母亲会用锡纸把鱼包起来，放一点盐和柠檬，再把烤盘推进炉子。她说那层银亮的纸能保住鱼肉的水分，不让表皮发干。有一回一位客人故意晚到，还带了道凉菜，想搅了这顿饭，可她那份从容正好衬出他的火气。他处处想跟她作对，让她的打算落空，她只是笑。锡纸破了一角，蒸汽一跑，整盘菜就毁了。她便再盖一层，重新推回炉里。旧盒子上的图，看着比我们这盘讲究多了。"},"grate":{"tw":[["grind",0],["chew",3],["noise",2],["grill",6],["scrape",0],["paw",3],["annoy",2],["chop",6],["fret",0]],"en":"On cold evenings my grandmother would kneel by the iron grate and lay the fire. The bars would grind against the coal as she turned them with a hook. A kettle hung above the flame, and the water never quite came to a boil. A cat would paw at the ashes and then chew a piece of dry bread beside the hearth. The noise of the wind in the chimney began to annoy her, and she would fret about the smoke. She had to scrape the soot off the grill every week and chop kindling into short sticks. The grate held the heat well, but it blackened every pot she set on it. Still, we sat there until the last coal fell.","zh":"天冷的晚上，我奶奶会跪在铁炉格前生火。她用钩子拨动炉条，铁条在煤上刮出响声。炉火上吊着一只水壶，水从没真正滚开过。一只猫用爪子扒着炉灰，然后蹲在炉边啃一块干面包。烟囱里风的响动开始让她心烦，她总为烟发愁。每周她都得把炉架上的烟灰刮掉，把引火的木柴劈成短段。这炉格很蓄热，可放在上面的每只锅都被熏得发黑。我们还是坐在那儿，一直坐到最后一小块煤塌下去。"},"hurl":{"tw":[["throw",2],["bowl",3],["express",2],["disperse",6],["cast",0],["crash",3],["move",2],["scatter",6],["thrust",0]],"en":"From the low bank, my brother would hurl flat stones across the water with a smooth turn of his wrist. Each throw was a small lesson in balance, and he loved to bowl them so they skipped. The bank was muddy, and he had to plant his feet wide before every turn. A single hurl could send a stone halfway across the pond. He would cast his arm back, then thrust it forward and watch the rings scatter. The wind would disperse the ripples before they reached the far side, and the birds would move off. Once a stone hit a rock with a sharp crash and broke in two. He said the water helped him express what he could not say.","zh":"我弟弟站在低低的河岸上，手腕一翻，把扁石用力掷过水面。每投一次都是一堂平衡课，他喜欢让石头贴着水蹦着走。岸边全是泥，每次出手前他都要把两脚叉开站稳。一下子就能把石头甩到池塘中间去。他先把胳膊往后一扬，再猛地往前送，看着一圈圈水纹散开。风会在波纹到对岸之前把它们吹散，鸟也就飞走了。有一次石头撞在岩石上，脆响一声，裂成两半。他说，水帮他讲出了说不出口的话。"},"ignite":{"tw":[["heat",0],["ferment",3],["burn",2],["extinguish",1],["spark",6],["light",0],["kindle",3],["flare",6],["inflame",0]],"en":"Before dawn the baker would ignite the wood in the brick oven and watch the first spark catch. He used a long strip of paper to light it, then let the flame flare up the chimney. In the warm room behind him the dough would ferment slowly and rise over the trays. A careless move could burn a sleeve, and once a spark was enough to inflame a whole sack of flour. He kept a wet cloth to extinguish any small fire before it could kindle the shelves. The heat would slowly fill the shop and warm the glass. He said the oven taught him patience more than any book.","zh":"天还没亮，面包师就点着砖炉里的木柴，看着第一点火星燃起来。他用一条长纸引火，让火苗顺着烟囱窜上去。身后暖屋里，面团慢慢发起来，胀满了一个个烤盘。稍不留神就会烧到袖子，有一次一点火星就引燃了整袋面粉。他总备着一块湿布，趁火还没烧到架子就把它按灭。热气一点点灌满铺子，把玻璃也烘暖了。他说这炉子教他的耐心，比任何一本书都多。"},"lash":{"tw":[["whip",0],["cat",3],["beat",2],["pummel",6],["strap",0],["switch",3],["blow",2],["sleet",6],["slash",0]],"en":"The driver would not use the lash on his old horse, even when the sleet began to beat against the cart. He kept the whip rolled under the seat and a leather strap tied to the rail. A cat slept in the straw behind them, unbothered by the wind. At the top of the hill the sleet turned to hard ice, and one blow of wind could pummel the canvas. He had to switch the reins from one hand to the other and slash a path through the drift. The road was a white line with no fence on either side. Under his lashes I saw it disappear. He said a man who beats an animal has learned nothing from the winter.","zh":"车夫从不肯用鞭子抽他那匹老马，哪怕雨雪已经开始打在车板上。他把鞭子卷起来塞在座位底下，一根皮条系在栏杆上。一只猫在后面的干草里睡着，风再大也不理。到了坡顶，雨雪变成硬硬的冰粒，一阵风就能把帆布抽得噼啪响。他只好把缰绳从一只手换到另一只手，在雪堆里劈开一条路。路成了一道白线，两边都没有栏。透过他的睫毛，我看见那道白线一点点消失。他说，一个动手打牲口的人，什么也没从冬天里学会。"},"erode":{"tw":[["erosion",4],["fret",0],["wash",3],["damage",2],["undercut",6],["gnaw",0],["decay",2]],"en":"Every winter the sea slowly erodes the soft cliff below our village. The erosion is easy to see from the path: whole stretches of grass have fallen away, and the waves have begun to undercut the base of the rock. Rain and salt wash the loose soil down to the shore, and the wind seems to gnaw at every exposed edge. Local people fret about the houses near the top, though the damage so far is limited to a fence and an old shed. Timber in the harbour shows the same slow decay. Engineers say a stone wall would help, but nobody has paid for one yet. From the path you can still see where the old fence once stood.","zh":"每年冬天，海水都在慢慢侵蚀我们村子下方那片松软的崖壁。从小路上就能看清侵蚀的痕迹：整片整片的草塌了下去，海浪已经开始掏空岩石的底部。雨水和盐分把松土冲到岸边，风也像在啃咬每一处裸露的边缘。当地人为崖顶附近的房子发愁，不过目前受损的只有一道篱笆和一间旧棚屋。港口里的木头也显出同样的缓慢腐朽。工程师说砌一道石墙会有用，可到现在还没人出钱。从小路上还能看出旧篱笆原来立在哪里。"},"generator":{"tw":[["generate",4],["source",0],["dynamo",3],["engine",2],["pump",6],["apparatus",2],["grid",6]],"en":"When the storm cut the power, the whole street went dark for six hours. Our neighbour had an old generator in his shed, and it took him a while to start the engine. The machine is a heavy apparatus of iron and wire, and its small dynamo hums like a bee when it runs. He uses it to generate enough current for his fridge and one lamp, and to pump water from the well. For most people the grid came back before midnight, but his house stayed bright. He says the generator is his only real source of comfort in a bad winter. In summer he services it himself, cleaning the filter and checking the oil.","zh":"暴风雨一停电，整条街黑了六个小时。邻居的棚子里有一台旧发电机，他花了好一会儿才把引擎发动起来。那机器是铁和线绕成的笨重装置，里面那个小直流发电机一运转就嗡嗡叫。他靠它发够电，供冰箱和一盏灯用，还能从井里抽水。大多数人家半夜前电网就恢复了，只有他家一直亮着。他说在难熬的冬天，这台发电机是他唯一真正的慰藉来源。"},"disgrace":{"tw":[["shame",0],["reduce",3],["humiliate",2],["utter",6],["degrade",0],["foul",3],["pity",6],["discredit",0]],"en":"Years later, the old rowing club still talked about the disgrace of that summer. A senior member had falsified the race records, and when the truth came out the whole team was reduced to silence. The coach did not shout; he said the fraud would discredit every honest win the club had ever had. He refused to humiliate the young rowers, who had done nothing wrong. Some neighbours pitied them, but pity only made the shame worse. One official tried to degrade the matter into a small clerical error, which everyone found foul. To call it that was an utter lie, and the member resigned that week without a word of apology. The trophy from that year was quietly put away in a cupboard.","zh":"多年以后，那家老赛艇俱乐部还在说那年夏天的丑事。一名老队员改了比赛记录，事情一露出来，整支队伍都沉默下来。教练没有吼，只说这种造假会让俱乐部所有干净的胜利都失去信任。他不肯去羞辱那些年轻队员，他们什么也没做错。有邻居可怜他们，可那点同情只让羞耻更重。有位负责人想把这件大事说成一个小小的登记错误，大家都觉得这说法很脏。把它说成那样，是彻头彻尾的谎话，那个队员当周就退了会，一句道歉也没有。那一年的奖杯被悄悄收进了柜子。"},"diverge":{"tw":[["vary",0],["branch",3],["move",2],["converge",1],["intersect",6],["deviate",0],["contradict",3],["resonate",6]],"en":"The path above the lake would diverge into two tracks just past the wooden bridge. One branched left toward the ridge, the other moved down to the water. We could not decide, and my brother's account of the map began to contradict mine. Our guesses varied with every step, and at one point a third trail seemed to deviate from the main line for no reason. Where the tracks finally intersect there is a flat stone, and the two routes converge again before the summit. We stood there a while, listening to a hollow sound that seemed to resonate under the rock. In the end both choices were fine, which is the trouble with any fork.","zh":"过了木桥，湖上那条小路就分开成两条。一条向左拐上山脊，另一条往下走到水边。我们拿不定主意，弟弟对地图的说法也开始跟我对不上。每走一步，我们的猜测都在变，有一处甚至有条第三条小路莫名地从主线岔出去。两条道最后交汇的地方有一块平石，在到山顶之前又重新合成一条。我们在那儿站了一会儿，听着石头底下有个空洞的声音在回响。到头来两个选择都没错，这大概就是岔路最麻烦的地方。"},"dodge":{"tw":[["duck",0],["plant",3],["move",2],["jeep",6],["hedge",0],["quibble",3],["avoid",2],["skirt",0]],"en":"Walking back along the lane, we had to dodge a jeep that came round the corner far too fast. My sister ducked behind the hedge, and I moved onto the grass verge. The driver did not stop to quibble about who had the right of way; he simply waved and drove on. We decided to avoid that road after dark and to skirt the field instead, past the low plant nursery. There was no point arguing over a few feet of gravel, so we let it go. Later we laughed about how quickly we had to move. The hedge still had a white mark where the wing mirror had brushed it, and the owner left it there for a month.","zh":"沿着小路往回走的时候，我们不得不躲开一辆拐弯拐得太快的越野车。妹妹蹲到树篱后面，我则退到草边上。司机没有停下来争谁有优先通行权，只是摆了摆手就开走了。我们决定天黑以后不走那条路，改从田边绕过去，经过那家矮矮的苗圃。为几尺碎石路争一场实在没意思，就算了。后来我们笑说，当时躲得可真快。树篱上还留着一道白印，是后视镜蹭过去的，主人让它留了整整一个月。"},"drape":{"tw":[["curtain",0],["festoon",3],["cover",2],["weave",6],["cloak",0],["blind",2],["velvet",6],["robe",0]],"en":"Backstage at the little theatre, the wardrobe room was full of drape and dust. A heavy velvet curtain had been taken down and lay across two chairs. Someone had festooned the mirror with paper stars, and a blind hung crooked at the high window. Every robe for the winter play had to cover a plain coat, so the seamstress would weave a thin gold thread along each hem. She kept an old cloak in the corner, too worn to use and too good to throw away. 'A drape is not just cloth,' she said. 'It decides how a person stands, where the light falls, and how much of the stage a body can fill.'","zh":"小剧场的后台，服装间里到处是垂布和灰。一幅厚重的丝绒幕布被卸下来，横搭在两把椅子上。有人用纸星星把镜子缠了一圈，高窗上的百叶帘歪歪地挂着。冬天那出戏的每件长袍都得罩在一件素色外套外面，所以裁缝会在每条下摆上织进一根细细的金线。墙角还留着一件旧斗篷，破得不能穿，又舍不得扔。她说，垂布不只是布，它决定一个人怎么站、光落在哪里、一副身子能占满多少舞台。"},"duplicate":{"tw":[["double",0],["counterpart",3],["copy",2],["validate",6],["extra",0],["reproduce",2],["compare",6],["repeat",0]],"en":"The clerk in the records office asked me to bring a duplicate of every form. He wanted a double set, he explained, because one copy stayed in the building and the other went to the district office. He would compare the two and validate each page with a small stamp. If anything was missing he simply asked me to repeat the signature on an extra sheet. 'A duplicate is not a spare,' he said. 'It is the counterpart of the original, and it has to match line for line.' We could not reproduce the old ink exactly, but the numbers were the same. He filed both sets in the same grey box.","zh":"档案室的办事员让我每份表格都带一份副本。他解释说，要成双的两套，因为一份留在这栋楼里，另一份送区办公室。他会把两份对着看，再在每页上盖个小章确认有效。要是缺了什么，他就让我在另一张纸上重签一次名。他说，副本不是备用的，它是原件对应的一份，得一行一行都对得上。旧墨水的颜色我们仿不出来，可数字是一样的。他把两套都归进了同一个灰盒子里。"},"elicit":{"tw":[["raise",0],["draw",3],["interpret",2],["engender",6],["extract",0],["deduce",2],["amplify",6],["arouse",0]],"en":"The oral exam was designed to elicit more than a list of facts. The teacher would raise a simple question, then wait, letting the silence draw an answer out of us. When a student gave a short reply, she would amplify it with a follow-up until the reasoning became clear. From a few details we had to deduce the rest, and to interpret a chart that was deliberately incomplete. Her manner did not arouse fear; it seemed to engender a strange sort of confidence. Afterwards she said she could always extract the truth from a nervous candidate. 'Questions,' she told us, 'are how you find out what someone really thinks.'","zh":"那场口试要引出来的，不只是一串事实。老师会提一个很简单的问题，然后等着，让沉默把我们心里的答案一点点拽出来。学生答得短，她就追问一句，把话放大，直到思路清楚为止。我们得凭几个细节推断其余部分，还要解读一张故意留空的图表。她的态度并不让人害怕，反倒生出一种奇怪的底气。事后她说，她总能从紧张的考生嘴里把真话取出来。她跟我们说，提问就是弄清楚一个人真正怎么想的方法。"},"empower":{"tw":[["authorise",0],["entitle",3],["appoint",2],["integrate",6],["invest",0],["enable",2],["strive",6],["endow",0]],"en":"The new advice centre was set up to empower people who had never spoken to a lawyer. Its charter would authorise two volunteers to give basic guidance, though it could not entitle them to represent anyone in court. The board decided to appoint a part-time manager and to integrate the service with the existing night shelter. A small fund was used to invest in a second phone line and a printer. The aim was to enable people to fill in their own forms without paying for help. The first month brought forty visitors, most of them older women with letters from the housing office. 'We cannot endow anyone with courage,' the manager said, 'but we can help them strive for it.'","zh":"新开的咨询点是为了让那些从没跟律师说过话的人也能自己拿主意。章程授权两名志愿者提供基本指导，但没有给他们出庭代理的资格。理事会决定聘一名兼职主管，并把这个服务和现有的夜间收容点合到一起。一笔小经费用来添了第二条电话线和一台打印机。目标是让人有能力自己填表，不必花钱请人。头一个月来了四十个人，多半是拿着住房部门来信的上了年纪的妇女。主管说，我们没法把勇气直接送给谁，但可以帮他们自己去争。"},"enlist":{"tw":[["engage",0],["recruit",3],["procure",2],["discharge",1],["persuade",6],["draft",0],["conscript",3],["advise",6]],"en":"When the river rose that spring, the village had to enlist every pair of hands it could find. The warden began to recruit students from the school and to engage two retired boatmen. He had to procure sandbags from a depot three miles away, and to persuade the shop to lend its truck. Nobody was conscripted or drafted by force; they came because the water was already in the lower street. A few were discharged from their shifts early so they could help. By evening the wall of bags had risen to the height of a man, and the water stopped at the last step. 'I cannot advise you to be brave,' the warden said, 'only to be careful.'","zh":"那年春天河水涨起来时，村里凡是有手的人都得拉来帮忙。管事的开始从学校招学生，又请了两位退休的船工。他得从三英里外的仓库弄来沙袋，还要说服那家店把卡车借出来。没有人是被强征或抽丁来的，他们来是因为水已经漫进了下街。有几个人提前下了班赶来帮忙。到傍晚，沙袋墙已经垒到一人高，水停在最后一层台阶下。管事的说，我不能劝你们勇敢，只能劝你们小心。"},"exacerbate":{"tw":[["aggravate",0],["inflame",3],["change",2],["escalate",6],["exasperate",0],["irritate",3],["anger",2],["alleviate",6]],"en":"One loose tile was enough to exacerbate a problem we had ignored all winter. Each storm seemed to aggravate the leak, and the damp began to inflame the old plaster near the window. We tried to change the bucket twice a day, but the stain only escalated up the wall. The bucket filled faster than we could empty it, and the carpet under the window had to be thrown out. My father was exasperated by the cost, and the noise of dripping irritated everyone at night. I angered him further by suggesting we wait until spring. In the end a single tube of sealant did more to alleviate the trouble than any argument. He fixed the tile himself on a dry Sunday.","zh":"一片松了的瓦，就足以让我们忽略了一冬的毛病变得更糟。每场风雨都像在加重那道漏痕，潮气又开始刺激窗边那片老灰泥。我们试着一天换两次桶，可水渍只是顺着墙往上爬。桶满得比我们倒得还快，窗下那块地毯最后只好扔了。父亲被这笔开销弄得火大，滴水声夜里吵得人人都烦。我提议等到春天再说，这让他更生气。最后是一管密封胶比任何争论都更能缓解问题。他在一个干爽的星期天自己把那片瓦补上了。"},"fasten":{"tw":[["fix",0],["hang",3],["change",2],["buckle",6],["secure",0],["stick",3],["attach",2],["hoist",6]],"en":"Before the storm we had to fasten the loose sheet on the shed roof. My uncle showed me how to fix each corner with a metal plate, then how to attach a rope so we could hoist the ladder safely. He would buckle the strap tight and check that every knot was secure. A strip of tape would stick to the frame only until the rain came, so he changed it for a stronger seal. We had to hang the spare boards on the wall, clear of the floor, and mark where each one belonged. The wind was already pulling at the edge of the roof. 'Fasten it twice,' he said, 'and then look at it again.'","zh":"暴风雨来前，我们得把棚顶那块松了的铁皮固定住。舅舅教我怎么用铁片把每个角压牢，再怎么系上绳子，好把梯子安全地吊上去。他会把带扣拉紧，再检查每个结是不是牢靠。一条胶带只能粘到下雨前，所以他换成了更结实的封条。我们还得把备用的木板挂到墙上，不占地面。他说，固定两遍，然后再看一遍。"},"fatigue":{"tw":[["tire",0],["exhaust",3],["devolve",2],["stress",6],["wear",0],["retire",3],["pain",6],["weary",0]],"en":"The night shifts on the ward left a fatigue that sleep could not quite clear. By the fourth night the younger nurses began to tire before midnight, and the oldest one looked utterly exhausted. The heaviest work seemed to devolve on whoever had the least experience. The stress showed in small ways: a forgotten note, a tray left in the corridor. Years of wear on the wooden floor had made a soft path from the desk to the beds. One nurse, close to retire, said the pain in her knees was worse than the weary feeling in her head. They all went home at dawn and slept through the morning light.","zh":"病房里的夜班留下一种睡多久也散不掉的疲乏。到第四个晚上，年轻护士不到午夜就开始犯困，年纪最大的那个看上去已经完全撑不住了。最重的活似乎总是落到经验最少的人身上。压力体现在小事上：一张忘了写的记录，一只落在走廊里的托盘。木地板被踩了这么多年，从桌前到床边磨出一条浅浅的路。一位快退休的护士说，膝盖的疼比脑子里那股乏劲还难受。天亮时她们都回了家，睡过了整个上午的光。"},"feast":{"tw":[["feed",0],["gaudy",3],["dinner",2],["ritual",6],["spread",0],["eat",2],["holiday",6],["banquet",0]],"en":"Every autumn the village held a feast in the old barn to mark the end of the harvest. Long tables were pushed together, and the spread of food seemed to cover half the floor. Neighbours would feed anyone who arrived, whether they had helped in the fields or not. My aunt thought the decorations were a little gaudy, but the children loved the paper lanterns. The dinner began with a short ritual: a cup passed from hand to hand. It was not a formal banquet, and nobody had to eat more than they wanted, though plates went back for second helpings all evening. By ten the holiday songs had started, and the barn doors were still open.","zh":"每年秋天，村里都会在老谷仓里摆一场宴席，庆祝收割结束。长桌一张张拼起来，铺开的吃食几乎占了半面地。邻居们谁来都管饭，不管有没有下过地。姑妈觉得那些装饰有点俗艳，可孩子们喜欢那些纸灯笼。晚饭前有个短短的仪式：一只杯子从一个人手里传到下一个人手里。那不算正式的宴会，谁也不必勉强自己多吃。到十点，节日的歌已经唱起来，谷仓的门还开着。"},"flake":{"tw":[["bit",0],["scale",3],["cover",2],["leach",6],["chip",2],["splinter",3],["form",2],["peel",0]],"en":"A flake of old paint came away under my thumb, and then another. The whole side of the boat had begun to peel in thin curls. I scraped until the loose scale was gone, and a small chip turned into a splinter of bare wood. Under the paint there was a dark form of rust where water had leached in for years. We had to cover the hull before the rain, so every bit of exposed wood was sanded and sealed. The yard smelled of turpentine and wet rope, and a bucket of scrapers stood by the fence. By the time the light went, half the hull was grey and clean, and my hands were sore.","zh":"一小片旧漆在我拇指下脱落，接着又是一片。船的一整侧都开始卷起薄薄的皮。我刮到松动的鳞状漆皮都掉干净，一个小缺口又裂成了一根木刺，露出底下的木头。漆下面有一块发暗的锈迹，是多年渗水留下的。我们得赶在下雨前把船身盖好，所以每一处露出的木头都打磨、上了封。到晚上我的手都酸了，可那面终于平了。"},"glitter":{"tw":[["shine",0],["shimmer",3],["look",2],["glitz",6],["gleam",0],["flash",2],["wig",6],["sparkle",0]],"en":"The costume shop before the school play was all glitter and noise. A silver wig hung on a stand and seemed to shine under the bare bulb. Every sequin would shimmer as the children turned, and a glass bead could flash like a small lamp. My daughter wanted the crown that had lost none of its glitz, though one side was held with tape. She would look at herself in the mirror for minutes, turning her head so the light would gleam on her cheek. The floor was covered with tiny silver dots that stuck to our shoes. 'A little sparkle is enough,' the seamstress said, and took the wig down.","zh":"学校演出前，那家服装店里到处是闪片和喧闹。一顶银色的假发挂在架子上，在光秃秃的灯泡下像是自己在发亮。孩子们一转圈，每片亮片都跟着晃出光，一颗玻璃珠子还能像小灯一样一闪。女儿想要那顶一点没失掉气派的王冠，虽然有一边是用胶带粘住的。她会在镜子前看好几分钟，转着头，让光落在脸颊上。裁缝说，一点亮就够了，说着把假发取了下来。"},"groom":{"tw":[["dress",3],["qualify",3],["participant",2],["bride",6],["prepare",0],["shave",3],["marry",6],["train",0]],"en":"On the morning of the wedding, the groom was quieter than anyone else in the house. He had shaved twice, and still he kept checking the mirror. His brother helped him dress, straightening the collar of a borrowed jacket. The bride's car was late, and the train of her dress had to be lifted over the wet steps. He did not feel qualified to give a speech, though he had prepared one for weeks. Only a few people knew how long the couple had waited to marry. 'A groom is not a participant in a ceremony,' his mother said. 'He is one half of it.' By noon the hall was full and he was laughing.","zh":"婚礼那天早上，新郎比屋里谁都安静。他刮了两遍胡子，还是不停地照镜子。哥哥帮他穿好衣服，把借来的外套领子理平。新娘的车晚了，她裙子的拖尾得抬起来才能过湿台阶。他觉得自己没资格致辞，尽管已经准备了好几个星期。只有少数几个人知道这对人等了多久才结婚。他母亲说，新郎不是婚礼上的一个参加者，他是婚礼的一半。到中午，厅里坐满了人，他也笑开了。"},"hack":{"tw":[["cut",2],["axe",3],["car",2],["rip",6],["chop",0],["horse",2],["whiz",6],["plug",0]],"en":"After the storm, a broken branch had come down across the drive, and we had to hack it into pieces small enough to move. My uncle brought an axe and showed me where to cut so the wood would not split wrong. Each chop sent a fine dust into the air, and a splinter could rip through a glove. We loaded the pieces into the car and drove them to the yard, where a horse stood watching from the fence. The saw would whiz through the thinner ends in seconds. The wood was still damp and heavier than it looked. Later I found a plug of wood stuck in the hinge of the gate.","zh":"暴风雨过后，一根断枝横在车道口，我们得把它砍成能搬动的小块。舅舅拿来一把斧子，教我从哪里下刀，木头才不会裂歪。每砍一下都扬起一层细末，一根木刺能把手套划破。我们把砍好的木块装进车里，运到院子里，一匹马站在栅栏边看着。锯子穿过细的那几截只要几秒钟。后来我发现门轴的缝里卡着一块木塞。"},"heighten":{"tw":[["raise",2],["fan",3],["increase",2],["inflame",6],["rise",0],["amplify",3],["aggravate",6],["compound",0]],"en":"The last ten minutes of the match seemed only to heighten the tension in the stand. Every missed pass would raise a groan, and the drums began to fan the noise into a steady roar. The crowd's anger seemed to increase with each whistle, and a careless word from the bench could inflame the row behind us. As the wind rose, the loudspeaker amplified every shout twice over. A decision that might have been forgotten was aggravated by the delay, and one mistake began to compound another. Two men near the tunnel began to shout at the referee, and the stewards moved closer. When the final whistle came, nobody moved.","zh":"比赛最后十分钟，看台上的紧张只是一味地往上升。每一次传丢都引来一片低声抱怨，鼓声把噪音扇成一片持续的轰鸣。人群的火气随着每一声哨响往上加，替补席上一句不慎的话就能把我们后面那排人点着。风起来的时候，喇叭把每一声喊都放大了一倍。一个本来会被忘掉的判罚因为拖延而变得更糟，一个错开始叠上另一个错。终场哨响时，没有一个人动。"},"hike":{"tw":[["raise",2],["trudge",3],["walk",2],["rate",6],["rise",0],["increase",2],["drop",6],["boost",0]],"en":"The autumn hike had been planned for months, but the club announced a hike in the fee at the last meeting. Fuel costs had risen, and the guide had to raise the rate for the bus that took us to the ridge. A rise in numbers would have helped, yet bookings took a drop after the notice went out. To boost interest, the club offered a shorter walk for families. On the day itself we trudged up a wet path for three hours, and the fog increased with every step. The hut at the top was full, and the tea tasted better than it ever had. Nobody complained about the money by the time we reached the top.","zh":"秋天的徒步早就计划好了，可俱乐部在最后一次会上宣布要涨费。油价涨了，向导只好把送我们上山脊的包车价提上去。人数要是能多些还好，可通知一发出，报名反倒少了。为了提起大家的兴趣，俱乐部又安排了一条给家庭走的短线。到了那天，我们在湿滑的路上跋涉了三个小时，雾一步一步地浓起来。等爬到顶上，已经没人再计较那点钱了。"},"hinder":{"tw":[["back",0],["check",3],["prevent",2],["impede",6],["block",0],["hang",3],["hamper",6],["embarrass",0]],"en":"Fallen trees and deep snow continued to hinder the delivery of food to the upper village. A lorry was stuck at the back of the line, and two more were blocked at the bridge. The drivers tried to check the depth with a pole, but the drift was too soft to measure. Ice on the slope would impede anyone on foot and hamper the carrying of heavy boxes, which had to be taken the last mile by hand. We could not prevent the delay, only shorten it. A rope was hanging from the wing mirror so the men could pull themselves along. One driver said the wait did not embarrass him half as much as the empty shelves would.","zh":"倒下的树和厚厚的积雪一直妨碍着往上面村子送粮。一辆卡车堵在车队末尾，另外两辆被拦在桥头。司机们想用杆子探探雪有多深，可雪堆太松，量不出来。坡上的冰会阻碍步行的人，也让搬重箱子变得艰难。这场延误我们阻止不了，只能想办法缩短。后视镜上垂着一根绳子，好让人拉着往前走。一位司机说，比起空着的货架，等这一会儿根本不算难堪。"},"hover":{"tw":[["linger",0],["poise",3],["fly",2],["soar",6],["loom",0],["hang",2],["descend",6],["vibrate",0]],"en":"The small drone would hover above the field for what felt like hours, its shadow moving slowly over the rows. It seemed to poise itself against the wind, then soar sideways and hang there, humming. A hawk would fly past once, annoyed, and the machine began to vibrate as it climbed. Far off, a dark cloud began to loom over the hills, and the light changed. We watched it descend at last, slowly, until it lingered a metre above the grass. The rotors threw a wide circle of dust across the rows. My father said a good pilot lets the machine hover, never forcing it. Then the battery warning sounded, and it dropped into his hands.","zh":"那架小无人机在田上方悬着，感觉有好几个小时，影子慢慢地从一行行作物上移过。它像是顶着风稳住自己，然后侧着升上去，停在那儿嗡嗡响。一只鹰不满地飞过一次，机器往上爬的时候就开始震。远处一团黑云压上山头，光线变了。我们看着它终于慢慢降下来，在草地上方一米处停了一会儿。父亲说，好飞手会让机器自己悬住，从不硬来。接着电量警报响了，它落进他手里。"},"howl":{"tw":[["roar",0],["thunder",3],["cry",2],["scream",6],["wail",0],["squeal",3],["laugh",2],["growl",6]],"en":"That night the wind began to howl around the corners of the house. The sea below sounded like a roar that would not stop, and the thunder came so close the windows shook. Our dog would cry at the door, then wail at the top of the stairs. My sister tried to laugh it off, but when a branch hit the roof she gave a short scream. The old gate would squeal on its hinge with every gust, and somewhere in the yard a fox began to growl. Nobody slept much, and the garden was full of broken twigs by first light. The storm passed just before dawn, and the dog slept with its head on the mat.","zh":"那天夜里，风开始在屋角外面嚎。下面的海像是一直不停的吼声，雷近得把窗户都震响了。我们的狗先在门口呜呜叫，后来又跑到楼梯口哀号。妹妹想笑着敷衍过去，可一根树枝砸到屋顶时，她还是短促地尖叫了一声。旧木门每被风一吹就在铰链上吱嘎响，院子某处有只狐狸开始低吼。到早上风暴过去了，狗把头搁在垫子上睡着。"},"immerse":{"tw":[["absorb",0],["dip",3],["penetrate",2],["acquaint",6],["plunge",0],["soak",3],["socialise",6],["steep",0]],"en":"For six weeks that summer I was immersed in a language course with no English allowed. We would plunge into a conversation before we knew the words, and simply absorb what we could. The teachers wanted us to soak up the sound the way a cloth soaks water. In the afternoons we had to socialise with local families, which was harder than any lesson. A word I did not know would penetrate my sleep, and by morning it made sense. We were steeped in the language from breakfast to dusk. I grew acquainted with my own mistakes, and slowly stopped fearing them. By the last week I could dip into a newspaper and follow the sense.","zh":"那年夏天有六个星期，我整个人泡在一门不许说英语的语言课里。我们常常还不知道词就先跳进一段对话，能吸收多少算多少。老师希望我们像布吸水一样把那些声音吸进去。下午我们得去和当地人家来往，那比任何一节课都难。一个不认识的词会钻进我的梦里，到早上忽然就通了。从早饭到天黑，我们都浸在这门语言里。我渐渐熟悉了自己的错误，也不那么怕它们了。到最后一个星期，我已经能随手翻开报纸看个大意。"},"implant":{"tw":[["plant",0],["pot",3],["attach",2],["transplant",6],["embed",0],["nest",3],["communicate",2],["surgical",6]],"en":"The surgical team explained that the implant would be embedded just behind the ear. It would attach to a small device outside, and in time it would help the boy communicate with his class. His mother had planted bulbs in a pot by the ward window, and a bird had built a nest on the ledge outside. 'We do not transplant anything,' the nurse said. 'We embed it and let the body accept it.' The operation took two hours. Afterwards, the boy slept with one hand over the bandage, and the nurse said he would hear the wind before he heard a voice. The bulbs in the pot began to show green.","zh":"外科团队解释说，这个植入体要嵌在耳朵后面。它会和外边一个小装置相连，慢慢帮男孩和班上的同学交流。他母亲在病房窗边的一个花盆里种了球茎，窗外窗台上还有鸟筑了巢。护士说，我们不是在移植什么，我们是把它嵌进去，让身体自己接受它。手术做了两个小时。之后男孩睡着了，一只手盖在绷带上，花盆里的球茎开始冒绿。"},"infuse":{"tw":[["steep",0],["draw",3],["fill",2],["wring",6],["impregnate",0],["din",3],["drill",2],["imbue",6]],"en":"At the tea shop, the owner would infuse each pot for exactly three minutes. She let the leaves steep in water just off the boil, then watched the colour draw out slowly. The room would fill with a smell that seemed to impregnate the curtains and the wooden shelves. Above the din of the street she would drill her new assistant on the order of the steps. 'Do not wring the leaves,' she said. 'Let them give what they have.' She wanted to imbue every cup with the same patience. The shop closed at six, and the last pot was always for herself. When the pot was empty, she would turn it over and tap it once.","zh":"在那家茶店里，老板娘每壶茶都只泡整三分钟。她让茶叶在刚离火的水里闷着，然后看着颜色一点点浸出来。屋里会充满一种气味，像是钻进了帘子和木架子里。街上的嘈杂声里，她还在教新来的帮手记步骤的顺序。她说，别去拧茶叶，让它们自己把有的东西交出来。她想让每一杯都带着同样的耐心。壶空了，她会把壶翻过来，轻轻敲一下。"},"inhale":{"tw":[["inspire",0],["puff",3],["smoke",2],["exhale",1],["suck",6],["sniff",3],["breathe",2],["ingest",6]],"en":"On the first cold morning of the year, the running coach told us to inhale through the nose and let the air warm before it reached the lungs. 'Breathe slowly,' he said. 'Do not suck the cold in.' We had to exhale through the mouth, counting four steps. A puff of steam hung in front of each face. One student had a habit of smoking before the run, and he would sniff and cough for the first mile. The coach warned that we should never ingest anything heavy within an hour of training. By the second mile the air no longer felt sharp. 'A good run should inspire you,' he said, 'not finish you.'","zh":"一年里第一个冷早晨，跑步教练让我们用鼻子吸气，让空气暖一点再进肺。他说，慢慢呼吸，别把冷气往里吸。我们得用嘴呼气，数四步。每个人面前都挂着一团白气。有个学生习惯跑前抽一支烟，头一英里总在吸鼻子、咳嗽。教练提醒我们，训练前一小时内别吃任何厚重的东西。他说，好的跑步应该让你振奋，不是把你跑垮。"},"lag":{"tw":[["jail",0],["drag",3],["cover",2],["anticipate",6],["meanwhile",0],["follow",2],["trend",6],["interim",0]],"en":"The work on the old jail had begun in spring, but by August there was a clear lag in the schedule. Rain had held up the roof, and every delivery seemed to drag a week behind. The builders tried to cover the open cells with plastic before each storm. They could not anticipate how long the stonework would take, so the opening date kept moving. Meanwhile, the town had found an interim use for the yard: a small market on Saturdays. The committee decided to follow the example of other small museums and open one wing first. The trend in such projects, they were told, is always to open late.","zh":"旧监狱的修缮春天就开工了，可到八月，进度明显落后。雨耽误了屋顶，每一批材料似乎都要拖后一个星期。工人们赶在每场雨前用塑料布把敞着的牢房盖住。他们估不准石活要多久，开放日期就一直往后挪。与此同时，镇上给院子找了个临时用途：星期六开个小集市。委员会决定照别的小博物馆的做法，先开一个侧翼。有人告诉他们，这类工程的惯例就是晚开。"},"lapse":{"tw":[["pass",0],["fly",3],["end",2],["justify",6],["sink",0],["mistake",2],["error",6],["regress",0]],"en":"At the end of a long shift, a small lapse in the checklist nearly cost our team a whole day. I had signed off a delivery without counting the boxes, a mistake I could not justify even to myself. The error sat in the report until a colleague caught it, and by then the truck had already passed the gate. For an hour I watched my confidence sink while the manager asked how the system could regress so easily. There was no excuse, only the plain fact that attention flies away when people are tired. I spent the last hour of the day rebuilding the count box by box, and I ended the shift with a short note on the board. The lapse was mine, and the lesson stayed.","zh":"一个长班快结束时，清单上的一处小疏漏差点让我们整个组白干一天。我没点箱数就签收了一批货，这个错误我连对自己都无法辩解。那份报告里就留着这个错，直到一位同事发现，而那时卡车早已开出了大门。有一个小时，我眼看着自己的信心往下沉，经理还问系统怎么会这么容易倒退。没有借口，只有一个简单的事实：人累了，注意力就会飞走。我把那天的最后一个小时用来一箱一箱重新清点，收工时在板上留了一张短条。疏漏是我的，教训也留了下来。"},"lure":{"tw":[["hook",3],["call",3],["provoke",2],["attract",6],["tempt",0],["seduce",3],["recruit",6],["bait",3]],"en":"My uncle keeps a box of hand-made lures, and every spring he tries to recruit me for a weekend at the lake. His favourite is a silver spoon with a single hook, a bait he swears no fish can resist. He will call me three times a week, describe the mist on the water, and tempt me with stories of huge catches. Last year he almost seduced me into buying a boat I could not afford. What finally attracted me was not the fishing but the quiet: no phone, no traffic, nothing to provoke a bad mood. I held the rod for two hours without a bite, watching the lure turn in the light. Then something struck the bait hard, and the line went tight.","zh":"舅舅有一盒手工做的鱼饵，每年春天他都想拉我一起去湖边过个周末。他最喜欢的是一个带单钩的银色亮片，他发誓没有鱼能抗拒这种饵。他一星期能给我打三次电话，描述水面上的雾，用大鱼的故事来诱惑我。去年他差点说动我买下一条我根本养不起的船。最后吸引我的不是钓鱼，而是那份安静：没有电话，没有车流，没有什么能惹出坏情绪。我握着竿站了两个小时，一口也没有，只看着鱼饵在光里转动。然后有东西重重地咬住了饵，线一下子绷紧。"},"lurk":{"tw":[["linger",0],["prowl",3],["hide",2],["wander",6],["lounge",0],["wait",2],["seethe",6],["ambush",0]],"en":"Every evening our neighbour's grey cat lurks behind the shed, waiting for the right moment to cross the yard. It will prowl along the fence, hide under the roses, and then freeze in a silent ambush near the bird bath. Our dog likes to lounge on the step, but the moment he sees that cat he begins to seethe, and his low growl lingers in the air. Yesterday the cat wandered too close, and the two of them stared at each other for a full minute. Nothing happened; the cat simply turned and walked off as if the whole yard belonged to it. I stood at the window and waited for the dog to calm down. Some evenings I think the cat enjoys the game more than the birds do.","zh":"每天傍晚，邻居家那只灰猫都潜伏在棚子后面，等着合适的时机穿过院子。它会沿着篱笆潜行，藏在月季下面，然后在鸟浴盆边一动不动地设下埋伏。我们的狗喜欢趴在台阶上懒着，可一看见那只猫就开始憋火，低低的呜咽在空气里久久不散。昨天猫走得太近了，两个家伙对视了整整一分钟。什么也没发生，猫只是转身走开，好像整个院子都归它。我站在窗边等狗平静下来。有些傍晚我觉得，这只猫享受这场游戏胜过那些鸟。"},"disintegrate":{"tw":[["decay",0],["run",3],["integrate",1],["deform",6],["decompose",0],["crash",3],["corrode",6]],"en":"The fishing boat on the mud below the harbour wall has been there since before I was born. Its wooden planks have begun to decay, and salt has corroded every metal fitting until the hinges are only brown flakes. In winter the hull would deform under the weight of the tide, and the paint would run down the side in long grey lines. Left alone, the wood will decompose into the mud within a few years. Some people say the town should integrate the wreck into a small museum, but nobody has found the money. One storm may finish the job and crash what is left against the stones. Watching it disintegrate, I understand why the old fishermen never called a boat a thing. They called it a name.","zh":"港墙下面泥滩上那条渔船，在我出生之前就在那儿了。它的木板已经开始腐朽，盐把每个金属件都蚀得只剩褐色的薄片。冬天船身在潮水的重量下会变形，油漆顺着船舷流成一道道灰线。没人管的话，这些木头几年内就会烂进泥里。有人说镇上该把这具残骸融进一个小博物馆，但没人找得到钱。一场风暴也许就能了结，把剩下的部分撞到石头上。看着它一点点解体，我明白为什么老渔民从不把船叫作东西。他们给它起名字。"},"dispense":{"tw":[["deal",3],["assign",3],["treat",2],["legislate",6],["lot",0],["exempt",2],["distribute",0]],"en":"At the clinic on the hill, a nurse dispenses free medicine every Tuesday to anyone who needs it. She has to distribute the boxes fairly, so she will deal with the urgent cases first and assign the rest a number. The supply is small, and the rules exempt only children and the very old from paying. She cannot legislate, of course, but she can decide how the lot is divided on a bad day. A man with a bad cough waited two hours and then tried to treat the queue as his personal audience, telling everyone what she should do. She listened, handed him his bottle, and asked him to come back on Friday. Afterwards she said the hardest part of the job is not the medicine but the fairness.","zh":"山上的诊所里，一位护士每周二给任何需要的人免费发药。她得把药公平地分出去，所以先处理急的，给其余的编个号。药不多，规定只让小孩和很老的人免付钱。她当然没法立法，但在艰难的日子里，这一批怎么分由她定。一个咳得厉害的男人等了两小时，然后想把队伍当成自己的听众，对所有人讲她该怎么做。她听完，把药瓶递给他，让他周五再来。事后她说，这活最难的地方不是药，而是公平。"},"ditch":{"tw":[["dump",0],["crash",2],["fence",6],["chuck",0],["abandon",2],["salvage",6],["trench",3]],"en":"On the lane behind the barn there is a deep ditch that fills with water every spring. Last month a boy on a bicycle took the corner too fast, hit the grass, and crashed into the fence beside it. He was not hurt, but the bike went over and landed in the ditch, half in the mud. His friends wanted to chuck it back onto the road, but the front wheel was bent. We had to dump the broken parts in a pile and carry the rest home. It looked like something to abandon, yet my uncle thought he could salvage the frame. He pulled it out of the trench, cleaned it, and straightened the wheel over two evenings. By Sunday the bike was running again, and the boy rode past the same corner very slowly.","zh":"谷仓后面那条小路上有条很深的沟，每年春天都积满水。上个月一个男孩骑自行车拐弯太快，冲到草地上，撞进了旁边的栅栏。他没受伤，可车子翻了过去，掉进沟里，一半陷在泥里。他的朋友想把车扔回路上，但前轮已经弯了。我们只好把坏掉的零件堆成一堆，其余的都搬回家。它看着像是该丢掉的东西，可叔叔觉得车架还能救。他把它从沟里拖出来，擦干净，用了两个晚上把轮子校直。到星期天车又能骑了，那男孩经过同一个拐角时骑得很慢。"},"doom":{"tw":[["sentence",0],["guarantee",2],["demise",6],["condemn",0],["declare",2],["spark",6],["designate",0]],"en":"When the mill announced it would close in June, the local paper declared it the end of an era. The manager read a short sentence from a sheet of paper, and the room went quiet. Two hundred jobs would go, and there was no guarantee of new work in the valley. The union called the decision a sentence of doom for the whole town, though others said the mill had been failing for years. Engineers had condemned the old roof and designated the east wing unsafe. What finally sparked the closure was a single repair bill that nobody would pay. The demise of the mill came slowly, then all at once, as such things do. Someone has already asked whether the empty floor could be used for something else.","zh":"当那家纺织厂宣布六月关门时，本地报纸说这是一个时代的终结。经理从一张纸上念了短短一句话，屋子里就静了。两百个岗位要没了，而山谷里并没有新工作的保证。工会把这一决定称作全镇的厄运判决，也有人说这家厂已经衰败多年。工程师早就判定旧屋顶不合格，把东翼划为危险区。真正引发关厂的，是一张没人愿意付的维修账单。工厂的消亡先是很慢，然后一下子全来了，这类事都是这样。已经有人在问，那片空车间能不能派上别的用场。"},"dread":{"tw":[["awful",0],["panic",3],["despair",6],["fear",2],["chill",3],["angst",6],["terrible",0]],"en":"For three weeks before my driving test I lived with a quiet dread that spoiled every meal. The night before, I lay awake and felt the old familiar fear climb up from my stomach. In the morning my hands were cold, and a chill ran through me as I sat in the car. The examiner was a large, calm man who said almost nothing, which was somehow more awful than a talkative one. Halfway through, I made a terrible turn and felt a wave of panic. A voice in my head began to whisper despair, telling me I had failed already. I took a breath, told the angst to be quiet, and finished the route. I passed, and the dread vanished in a second.","zh":"考驾照前的三个星期，我一直揣着一种安静的恐惧，连吃饭都没滋味。考前一晚我躺着没睡，感到那种熟悉的害怕从胃里往上爬。早上我手是凉的，坐进车里时一股寒意穿过全身。考官是个又高又沉静的男人，几乎不说话，这反倒比爱聊天的更让人难受。开到一半我拐了个很糟的弯，一阵慌乱涌上来。脑子里有个声音开始念叨绝望，说我已经挂了。我吸了口气，让那点焦虑闭嘴，把路线开完。我过了，那股恐惧一秒钟就没了。"},"embark":{"tw":[["enter",0],["board",2],["disembark",1],["undertake",6],["ship",0],["commence",6],["venture",0]],"en":"At six in the morning we embarked on a journey that had taken a year to plan. The ship was smaller than the photographs had suggested, and the smell of diesel filled the air as we began to board. My father had agreed to undertake the job of carrying all the maps, and he checked them twice before we entered the cabin. The captain said we would embark within the hour and disembark at the northern port before dark. Nobody was allowed to venture onto the deck until the ropes were pulled in. At seven the engines commenced their low, steady shaking, and the harbour began to slide away. My mother stood at the rail and said she had never been so happy to leave a place. I stayed there until the last light went.","zh":"早上六点，我们踏上了一段筹划了一年的旅程。船比照片上看着小，我们开始登船时，空气里全是柴油味。父亲承担了保管所有地图的任务，进舱前他把地图查了两遍。船长说我们一小时内起航，天黑前在北面的港口下船。绳子收回来之前，谁都不许冒险上甲板。七点时引擎开始低沉而稳定地抖动，港口慢慢往后退去。母亲站在栏杆边说，她从没这么高兴离开一个地方。我在那儿一直站到最后一缕光消失。"},"fiddle":{"tw":[["play",2],["slack",3],["repair",2],["accordion",6],["monkey",0],["flute",6],["toy",0]],"en":"My grandfather's fiddle had been in the attic for years, and last weekend I carried it down to repair it. The strings were slack, the bridge had fallen flat, and for two evenings I could only fiddle with the pegs and wait for the glue to dry. He used to play at family weddings, until the accordion took over every party and the flute was left in its case. Beside it lay a toy accordion, the one he gave me when I was six, still squeezing out a thin tune. My nephew kept trying to monkey with the tuning keys, so I sent him to the garden. On the third evening the old thing finally held its note, and the whole house went quiet. Nobody clapped; my grandmother stood in the doorway and smiled, which was better.","zh":"外祖父的那把小提琴在阁楼上放了好多年，上周末我终于把它搬下来修理。琴弦松了，琴码也塌了，头两个晚上我只能拨弄琴轴，等胶水干透。他以前常在家族婚礼上拉琴，后来手风琴占了每一场聚会，长笛就被搁回盒子里了。旁边还放着一只玩具手风琴，是他六岁时给我的，如今拉起来仍能哼出一段细细的调子。小侄子老想乱拨调音的弦轴，我便打发他去院子里。第三个晚上，这把老琴终于把音稳住了，整栋房子都静下来听。没人鼓掌；外祖母只是站在门口笑，这比鼓掌更好。"},"flare":{"tw":[["flame",0],["burn",2],["ignite",6],["flash",0],["fire",2],["trigger",6],["erupt",0]],"en":"The summer the hill caught fire, we watched the flare from the ridge above the village. It began as a small flame near the path, then a bright flash as the dry grass ignited all at once. Every few minutes the wind would trigger a new front, and the whole slope seemed to erupt in orange. Crews cut a line through the brush while the fire burned toward the stream. My uncle, who had fought such blazes for years, said one careless match could set a hillside alight, and that a single flare of wind could turn a quiet night into a disaster. By dawn the burning had stopped at the water. He walked the black edge with a torch, looking for any last spark, and found none.","zh":"山坡起火那个夏天，我们站在村子上方的山脊上看那片火光。它起初只是小路边的一小簇火苗，接着干草一下子被点着，腾起一片刺眼的亮光。每隔几分钟，风就催出新的火线，整面坡仿佛都在橘色里喷发。灭火队在林间砍出一条隔离带，火则一路烧向溪水。我舅舅跟这种火打了多年交道，他说一根不小心的火柴就能点着整片山坡，而一阵突起的风就能把安静的夜变成灾难。天亮时，火在水边停住了。他举着火把沿黑色的边缘走，寻找最后的火星，一颗也没找到。"},"flop":{"tw":[["right",0],["fail",2],["reel",6],["collapse",2],["descend",2],["flip",6],["bust",0]],"en":"Our school's spring play was meant to be a comedy, but it turned into a flop on the first night. The lead forgot every line, the lights went out in the second act, and the audience began to reel with embarrassment instead of laughing. A cardboard wall collapsed onto the piano, and the curtain descended while two actors were still arguing behind it. I had a small part and spent the evening waiting to flip a sign that nobody could read from the back rows. The reviewer in the school paper was kind, but the truth is that the whole thing was a plain bust: the jokes failed, and forty of the sixty seats went to parents. Still, we did one thing right, and that was to keep going until the last scene. The audience clapped out of relief, and we took our bows like survivors.","zh":"学校的春季话剧本该是出喜剧，结果头一晚就砸了。主角把台词忘得一干二净，第二幕灯又灭了，观众不是笑，而是尴尬得发晕。一面纸板墙塌到钢琴上，幕布落下时还有两个演员在后面争。我只有个小角色，整晚就等着翻一块后排谁也看不清的牌子。校刊的评论写得很客气，可事实是整场戏就是一场彻底的败笔：卖出六十个座位，四十个是家长。不过我们有一件事做对了，就是一直撑到最后一幕。观众鼓掌是松了口气，我们像幸存者一样谢了幕。"},"fuss":{"tw":[["bother",0],["care",2],["cringe",6],["mother",0],["worry",2],["joke",6],["trouble",0]],"en":"My mother made a great fuss about the first dinner my brother cooked for us, and half of it was worry rather than criticism. She would stand by the stove, ask about the salt twice, and cringe at the way he held the knife. He told her not to bother, that he did not care about perfection, and that a joke would help more than advice. The trouble came when the oven door stuck and the roast began to smoke. For ten minutes the kitchen was pure fuss: towels waving, windows open, three people talking at once. Then the smoke cleared, the meat was fine, and we ate with the windows still open. My brother says he will cook again next month, and this time nobody is allowed to mother him.","zh":"弟弟第一次给我们做饭，母亲为这顿饭大张声势，一半是操心，一半才是挑毛病。她守在灶边，把盐问了两遍，看他握刀的姿势还直皱眉。弟弟叫她别忙了，说他不在乎做得多完美，讲个笑话比提建议管用。麻烦出在烤箱门卡住、烤肉开始冒烟的时候。那十分钟里厨房乱成一团：毛巾乱挥，窗户全开，三个人同时说话。后来烟散了，肉其实正好，我们就开着窗吃完了。弟弟说下个月还要做，这一回谁也不许再像当妈似的管他。"},"harness":{"tw":[["rule",0],["control",2],["hoist",6],["tackle",0],["support",2],["rope",6],["rein",0]],"en":"At the stables where I worked one summer, every horse had its own harness hanging on a peg, and mine was a heavy thing of leather and brass. My job was to hoist it onto the back of the old gray mare, check every strap, and make sure the collar would support the weight of the cart. The farmer would tackle the buckles himself, muttering that a loose rope was worse than no rope at all. He said a harness is a kind of rule: it does not control the animal so much as agree with it. When the mare pulled, the rein had to answer gently, or the whole cart would swing. I learned more about patience in that yard than in any classroom.","zh":"我打暑期工的那个马厩里，每匹马都有一套挽具挂在木钉上，分给我的那套是皮革加黄铜的沉家伙。我的活儿是把它举上那匹老灰马的背，逐条检查皮带，还得确保颈圈能撑住车子的重量。农场主总要自己去对付那些带扣，一边嘟囔说松了的绳子比没绳子更糟。他说挽具其实是一种规矩：它并不是去控制马，而是与马达成一致。母马一使劲，缰绳就得柔和地回应，否则整辆车都会歪。我在那个院子里学到的耐心，比在任何教室里都多。"},"heave":{"tw":[["lift",0],["blow",2],["lob",6],["raise",0],["move",2],["prick",6],["gasp",0]],"en":"The ferry was loaded by hand that morning, and every crate had to be lifted onto the deck with a single heave. Two dock workers would raise each box, swing it once, and lob it toward the stack while the wind began to blow from the west. I tried to help and felt a sharp prick in my shoulder, then heard a gasp from the man beside me as a crate slipped. We had to move the whole load again so the weight would sit lower. Nobody said much; the work was steady and the sea was getting rough. By the time the last box was tied down, my arms were shaking. The crossing was short, but I have rarely been so glad to stand still.","zh":"那天早上渡船全靠人力装货，每只木箱都得一口气举上甲板。两个码头工人把箱子抬起来，晃一下，再往货堆那边抛，风这时候开始从西边刮起来。我也想帮忙，肩头忽然一阵刺痛，接着旁边那人倒抽一口气——一只箱子滑了。我们只好把整批货重新挪一遍，让重量压得更低。没人多说什么；活儿一直不停，海也渐渐起了浪。等最后一只箱子绑好，我的胳膊已经在抖。航程很短，可我很少那样庆幸能站着不动。"},"herald":{"tw":[["announce",0],["tell",2],["tribune",6],["predecessor",0],["greet",2],["gazette",6],["hail",0]],"en":"The town's little gazette has a new editor, and her first issue was a herald of change. She would announce every village meeting on the front page, tell readers why the bus route mattered, and greet each shopkeeper by name on her rounds. Her predecessor had run the paper for thirty years and preferred quiet lists to stories. She calls the old man the paper's tribune, the voice of the square, and he pretends not to like it. People hail her in the street now, and she stops to take notes. Last week she printed a piece about the flooded lane, and the council fixed the drain within days. A paper should herald what is coming, she told us, not only what has already happened.","zh":"镇上那份小报换了新主编，她的第一期就是一个变化的先声。她把每场村民会议都登在头版，告诉读者公交线路为什么重要，走访时还能叫出每个店主的名字。她的前任办了三十年报纸，偏爱安静的清单，不爱讲故事。她称那位老人是这份报的护民官、广场的声音，老人假装不爱听。如今街上的人见了她会高声招呼，她就停下来记笔记。上周她写了积水小巷的报道，几天之内市政就把下水道修好了。她对我们说，报纸应该预告将要发生的事，而不只是记录已经发生的事。"},"hum":{"tw":[["buzz",0],["teem",3],["noise",2],["bang",6],["seethe",0],["sing",2],["twitch",6]],"en":"The server room behind our office never goes quiet; there is always a low hum from the cooling units. On a normal day the machines buzz like a hive, and the noise is steady enough to forget. But last Tuesday something began to bang inside one rack, and the room seemed to seethe with heat. A technician watched a cable twitch against the panel and said the fans would sing a higher note as the temperature climbed. The floor under our feet seemed to teem with warm air. We moved two servers to the spare rack, and by evening the hum had dropped back to its old level. The room was dull and healthy again, and I found that I missed the noise.","zh":"办公室后面的机房从来静不下来，冷却机组总在低低地嗡嗡响。平常日子里机器像蜂箱一样嗡鸣，那种噪音稳定得让人忘了它的存在。可上周二，有个机柜里开始砰砰作响，整个房间仿佛热得要沸腾。技术员盯着面板上一根抽动的线缆说，温度再升，风扇就会唱出更高的调子。脚下的地板似乎都涌着热气。我们把两台服务器挪到备用机柜，到傍晚那阵嗡鸣又回到了原来的高度。房间重新变得沉闷而健康，我发现自己竟有点想念那点噪音。"},"icon":{"tw":[["picture",0],["graphic",3],["symbol",2],["legend",6],["image",0],["scan",3],["idol",6]],"en":"My grandmother's phone screen is a wall of icons, and each one is a small picture she has chosen herself. She keeps a graphic of a red flower for her garden notes, a tiny image of her dog for the photo album, and a blue square that opens the weather for the week. Among her friends she is a legend for learning all this at eighty. When she cannot find something, she asks me to scan the screen and point. Her real idol is not on the phone at all: it is a paper calendar by the door, marked in pencil. Still, she has learned that a symbol can be a promise, a small square that takes her somewhere. Last week she made her own icon for the doctor's number, and she was prouder of it than of anything I have built.","zh":"外祖母的手机屏幕是一整面图标，每一个都是她自己挑的小图画。她给园艺笔记配了一朵红花的图形，给相册配了一张狗的小图，还有一个蓝色方块，点开就是一周的天气。在朋友中间，她八十岁学会这些，已经成了个传奇。找不到东西时，她就让我扫一眼屏幕替她指。她真正崇拜的东西并不在手机里：那是门边一本纸质日历，用铅笔标着记号。不过她已明白，一个符号也可以是一种承诺，一个小方块就能把她带到某处。上周她给医生的号码做了自己的图标，比我做过的任何东西都让她得意。"},"intermediate":{"tw":[["average",0],["chemical",2],["terminal",1],["grade",6],["medium",0],["high",6],["mediate",0]],"en":"Our language school sorts students into three levels, and I was placed in the intermediate class, which is exactly where I belonged: better than average, far from fluent. The teacher would mediate whenever two of us argued about grammar, and she kept the pace at a medium speed so nobody was lost. On the first day we read a short piece about a chemical spill and had to explain it in our own words. My grade on that exercise was high, which surprised me. By December I could follow the news on the radio, though the terminal scenes of the film we watched still went past me. The step from intermediate to advanced, she warned, is the longest one, and most people stop halfway.","zh":"我们那所语言学校把学生分成三个等级，我被分到中级班，这正好是我的位置：比平均好一些，离流利还差得远。我们俩为语法争起来时，老师总会居中调停，并且把进度保持在中等速度，不让任何人掉队。第一天我们读了一篇关于化学品泄漏的短文，还得用自己的话讲一遍。那次练习我得了高分，倒让我意外。到十二月我已经能听懂电台新闻，可我们看的那部电影结尾的几场戏还是听不明白。她提醒说，从中级到高级是跨度最大的一步，多数人走到一半就停了。"},"jog":{"tw":[["clip",0],["continue",2],["tee",6],["trot",0],["push",2],["stroll",6],["nudge",0]],"en":"My doctor suggested a slow jog three times a week, so I began with a short loop around the park at a gentle trot. The first week I could barely continue past the gate, and a man in a red tee passed me twice with an easy clip. I would push myself to the next lamp post, walk for a minute, then nudge myself into a jog again. By the third week I could add the small hill, and by the fifth I was passing the bench where I used to stop. On rest days I take a long stroll instead, which my knees prefer. My neighbour says I look lighter, and I have stopped checking the clock. The loop is still short, but it belongs to me now.","zh":"医生建议我一周慢跑三次，我便从公园里一小圈开始，用很轻的步子小跑。第一周我几乎跑不过大门，一个穿红T恤的男人以轻松的步速超了我两回。我就逼自己跑到下一根路灯，走一分钟，再推自己重新跑起来。到第三周我能加上那座小坡，第五周已经跑过从前总要停下的长椅。休息日我改成长时间散步，膝盖更喜欢这样。邻居说我看着轻快了些，我也不再盯着钟看。这一圈仍然很短，但它现在属于我了。"},"liquor":{"tw":[["booze",0],["whiskey",3],["alcohol",2],["drink",6],["gin",3],["liquid",2]],"en":"At my cousin's wedding the bar opened before the ceremony ended, and the smell of liquor reached the back rows. An uncle who never touches alcohol spent the evening holding the same glass of orange liquid so people would stop asking. Two friends argued quietly about whiskey and gin, then went back to dancing as if nothing had happened. The bartender kept the booze behind a low wooden counter and poured every drink with a small measure. I stayed with water until the toasts, then took one glass of wine and left it half full. What I remember of that night is not the drinking but the sound of a hundred people talking at once. By midnight the hall was quiet, and the last bottles went back into the cupboard.","zh":"表姐的婚礼上，仪式还没完吧台就开了，酒气一直飘到后排。一位从不沾酒的叔叔整晚端着同一杯橙色饮料，好让别人别再来劝。两个朋友低声争论威士忌和杜松子酒哪个好，随后又像什么都没发生一样回去跳舞。调酒师把酒藏在矮木柜台后面，每杯都只倒一小份。我一直喝水，直到敬酒时才拿了一杯葡萄酒，还留了半杯。那晚我记得的不是喝酒，而是一百个人同时说话的声音。到午夜，大厅安静下来，剩下的瓶子都收回了柜子。"}}});
